    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "361caa89_69fb9861",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1643,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002751
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T00:05:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My next version will lint everything and product zip files of the results if you build `m lint-check`.  A few other options:\nWe could have phony targets for each module (`m Settings-lint`).\nWe could allow individual modules to turn on lint in all builds, although that would probably insert lint in the build graph between the module and its dependencies, slowing down the build.",
      "parentUuid": "2bb47ec3_b72d6045",
      "revId": "a4bd44285a7e32c0cfe9ef90075289da9cc6d89e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e7009927_76672cf2",
        "filename": "java/java.go",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 1643,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061164
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-08T16:43:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "none of this needs to come now.\n\n+1, if we expect people to work and fix lint issues, we will need phony targets so they can focus on their own issues.\n\nAs long as it is on presubmit, it should be fine for now? We would still prevent regressions. That\u0027s how its setup for most of google3. If we ever want it to be part of build, we should try to make it smarter: for example, not check transitive library sources since those were already checked.",
      "parentUuid": "361caa89_69fb9861",
      "revId": "a4bd44285a7e32c0cfe9ef90075289da9cc6d89e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
